      "id": "final-sale-damaged-exception",
      "category": "multi-source-grounding",
      "passed": false,
      "error": "",
      "agent_errors": [],
      "final_answer": "I\u2019m sorry you received a bag with a broken zipper.\u202fEven though the bag was sold as\u202f**final\u2011sale**, that label does **not** remove the limited warranty for a manufacturing defect, and final\u2011sale items that arrive damaged are still eligible for assistance under our Damaged or Wrong Items process.\n\n**What the policies say**\n\n* **Final\u2011sale products** \u2013 \u201cA product being marked final sale does not remove the limited warranty for a qualifying manufacturing defect.\u201d (07\u2011warranty.md \u2014 Final-sale products)  \n* **What is covered** \u2013 The limited warranty covers \u201cmanufacturing defects in materials or workmanship \u2026 such as a zipper mechanism that fails because of a manufacturing defect.\u201d (07\u2011warranty.md \u2014 What is covered)  \n* **Exclusions and exceptions** \u2013 \u201cFinal\u2011sale items \u2026 Damaged or incorrect final\u2011sale items may still qualify for assistance under the Damaged or Wrong Items Policy.\u201d (01\u2011returns-policy-current.md \u2014 Exclusions and exceptions)  \n* **Damaged or incorrect items** \u2013 \u201cThe final\u2011sale restriction does not remove a customer\u2019s right to report an item that arrived damaged, defective, or different from what was ordered.\u201d (03\u2011final-sale-and-promotions.md \u2014 Damaged or incorrect items)\n\n**What you can do**\n\n1. Gather your proof of purchase and clear photos of the broken zipper.  \n2. Contact our support team (via the \u201cHelp\u201d link in your order email or by calling\u202f1\u2011800\u2011555\u20110199). Let them know the bag is a final\u2011sale item that arrived defective.  \n3. The support specialist will open a warranty/damaged\u2011item claim, verify the defect, and guide you through the next steps (e.g., a replacement or repair).\n\nWe can\u2019t process the claim directly here, but the above policies confirm you are **not out of luck**\u2014you\u2019re eligible for warranty assistance despite the final\u2011sale label.\n\nIf you need help starting the claim or have any other questions, please let me know or reach out to a human support specialist.",
